      "side": 1,
      "message": "The KSO13 and KSO14 are used for the numpad. A keyboard without a numpad doesn\u0027t need the KSO13 and KSO14 muxed as alternative keyboard pins so these pins can be used as general GPIOs, like Herobrine does.\n\nAs this is a common npcx9 dts, I think it should keep a minimal set, i.e. removing the KSO13 and KSO14. For the projects which have numpads, they can override pinctl in their board dts files. Please add a comment to explain it.",
